    2. Choose n_sprites (2-3) and each sprite's lattice dims (along 1-3, cross 1-3). Keep cross dims identical.
    3. Compute frame logical dims from formulas (along = sum(sprite_along) + 2, cross = max(sprite_cross) + 1 or more, with cross != along to ensure non-square).
    4. Place frame at a random (odd,odd) anchor so the pixel bbox fits within [0,24]x[0,24].
    5. Fill the 25x25 grid with the bg+lattice checkerboard pattern.
    6. Stamp sparse frame perimeter onto (odd,odd) sub-lattice positions.
    7. For each sprite, choose a random (even,even) anchor outside the frame bbox (non-overlapping with frame and other sprites), and stamp its filled-rectangle sparse pixels.
    8. Verify sprites have unique ordering keys (no ties in col for horizontal, row for vertical).
